    {
      "id": "class05_01_english_103_learn_25_83b14bae",
      "type": "poem",
      "text": "1.\t\t\t                    Colours\nYou have a few crayons,\nRed, yellow and blue.\nGreen, purple and black,\nI have some too\nI need the red\nand you need the black.\nIf we share our crayons,\nwe have a full pack!\n– Santoor, Grade 3",
      "answer": null,
      "source": {
        "file": "01_LEARN\\01_LESSONS\\LESSONS.json",
        "page": 5
      },
      "order": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "class05_01_english_103_learn_26_8bb5e03c",
      "type": "poem",
      "text": "2.\t\t\t                    Aachoo!\nOnce a mighty elephant,\nGot a mighty cold.\nIt went to buy a handkerchief,\nWhere handkerchiefs were sold.\n“A hanky for an elephant?”\nThe sales girl was surprised,\n“Sorry sir but we don’t have\nA handkerchief that size.”\n“AACHOO!” said the elephant.\nAnd shook its mighty head,\n“Forget about the handkerchief\nGive me a sheet instead.”\n– Santoor, Grade 3",
      "answer": null,
      "source": {
        "file": "01_LEARN\\01_LESSONS\\LESSONS.json",
        "page": 5
      },
      "order": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "class05_01_english_103_learn_27_2143ebac",
      "type": "poem",
      "text": "Note       You may recite another poem in ‘different’ voices to\ndemonstrate different emotions. Ask learners about\nto the     feelings that the person reciting the poem is trying to\nTeacher    convey. Draw their attention towards gestures and\nexpressions. Learners may recite the poems individually\nor in pairs.",
      "answer": null,
      "source": {
        "file": "01_LEARN\\01_LESSONS\\LESSONS.json",
        "page": 5
      },
      "order": 28
    },
